{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/focussystem"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Focus System","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigate between interactive elements using the keyboard."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides a focus system that lets users move between interactive views (buttons, menus, text fields) using Tab, Shift+Tab, or arrow keys. The system consists of three parts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Tracks which element is focused, handles navigation"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable","isActive":true}]},{"type":"text","text":": Protocol that views adopt to receive focus"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Lightweight state object that views use to query and request focus","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"How-Focus-Works","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"How Focus Works"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every frame, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is cleared and interactive views re-register themselves during rendering. This means focus registrations are always in sync with the current view tree: removed views are automatically unregistered.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The focus order follows the rendering order: the first focusable view rendered is first in the Tab cycle."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Focusable-Protocol","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Focusable Protocol"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Views that want to receive focus conform to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public protocol Focusable: AnyObject {","    var focusID: String { get }","    var canBeFocused: Bool { get }","    func onFocusReceived()","    func onFocusLost()","    func handleKeyEvent(_ event: KeyEvent) -> Bool","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"focusID","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Unique identifier for this focusable element","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"canBeFocused","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Whether focus can move to this element (default: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFocusReceived()"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Called when this element gains focus (default: no-op)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFocusLost()"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Called when this element loses focus (default: no-op)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Handle a key event while focused; return ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" if consumed","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A default extension provides sensible defaults for ","type":"text"},{"code":"canBeFocused","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"onFocusReceived()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"onFocusLost()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (both no-ops). Only ","type":"text"},{"code":"focusID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must be implemented.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Using-FocusState","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Using FocusState"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState"},{"text":" is the user-facing API for checking and requesting focus inside a view:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let focusState = FocusState(id: \"my-button\", focusManager: context.environment.focusManager)","","\/\/ Check if this element is currently focused","if focusState.isFocused {","    \/\/ render with focus indicator","}","","\/\/ Programmatically request focus","focusState.requestFocus()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in views like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Button","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Menu","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" create their own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusState"},{"text":" internally: you only need it when building custom focusable views.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Navigation-Keys","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Navigation Keys"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" responds to these keys during dispatch:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tab"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the next element","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shift+Tab"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the previous element"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow Down \/ Right","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the next element","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow Up \/ Left","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the previous element"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"anchor":"FocusRegistration-Helper","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"FocusRegistration Helper"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in interactive views use the internal ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusRegistration"},{"text":" helper to avoid boilerplate. It handles three tasks in one call:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist a focus ID"}]},{"text":" via ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it remains stable across renders","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Register","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the handler with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Query"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" whether this view currently has focus","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom views that implement "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable"},{"type":"text","text":" typically do not need "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusRegistration"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. It is used by the framework’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_*Core"},{"type":"text","text":" views (e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_ButtonCore"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_ListCore"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Focus-Indicator","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Focus Indicator"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The visual indicator depends on the view type. Buttons and similar controls use a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"highlight background bar","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for the focused item. Text fields use "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pulsing vertical bars"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (caps) around the input area. Lists and tables use a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"highlight background","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for the focused row, with a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pulsing accent background"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when the row is both focused and selected."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Focus-in-the-Event-Loop","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Focus in the Event Loop"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Focus dispatch happens in Layer 2 of the key event pipeline (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppLifecycle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A key event arrives from stdin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer 1 (status bar) gets first chance to handle it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Layer 2: ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyEventDispatcher","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dispatches to the focused view’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If not consumed, navigation keys (Tab, arrows) are handled by ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer 3 (default bindings) handles quit, theme cycling, etc."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ImageDecoding"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/StatusBarGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","title":"Status Bar","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure the shortcut bar at the bottom of the terminal."}],"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/statusbarguide"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/AppearanceAndColors":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Control border styles, visual appearances, and the color system."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/appearanceandcolors","title":"Appearance and Co